@node Overview
@chapter Overview

@cindex overview
@cindex structure editing, idea

@LaTeX{} Structure ports the structure editing commands of Org mode to
@LaTeX{} buffers.  It treats the sectioning commands @code{\part} through
@code{\subparagraph} as Org headlines.  It treats the items of @code{itemize},
@code{enumerate}, and @code{description} environments as Org plain list items.

With the package you can do the following.

@itemize
@item
Refile a section under any heading of the document, in this file
or in another chapter file, with @code{C-c C-w}.  Heading levels change
to fit the new parent.
@item
Jump to any heading of the document with @code{C-u C-c C-w}.
@item
Show one section alone in an indirect buffer with @code{C-c C-x b}.
@item
Build a sparse tree of the lines that match a regexp with @code{C-c /}.
@item
Move, indent, and outdent list items with the Meta-arrow keys, and
cycle a list between @code{itemize}, @code{enumerate}, and @code{description} with
@code{C-c -}.
@item
Move, promote, and demote sections with the same Meta-arrow keys
that Org uses.
@end itemize

The package works with the built-in @code{latex-mode} and with the
@code{LaTeX-mode} of AUC@TeX{}.  It needs no other package.

@menu
* Relation to latex-speed-commands::
* Org commands and their analogs::
@end menu

@node Relation to latex-speed-commands
@section Relation to latex-speed-commands

@cindex latex-speed-commands
@cindex companion package

@LaTeX{} Structure is a companion to @LaTeX{} Speed Commands, which gives
@LaTeX{} the single-key speed commands of Org.  The two packages are
independent.  When both are loaded, the command
@code{latex-structure-speed-commands-setup} adds speed keys for refiling,
sparse trees, and list items.  See @ref{Speed commands}.

