@node Functions for Lisp code
@chapter Functions for Lisp code

@cindex Lisp interface
@cindex API
@findex latex-structure-section-bounds
@findex latex-structure-item-at
@findex latex-structure-master-file

A few functions are useful in your own commands.

@itemize
@item
@code{(latex-structure-section-bounds)} returns @code{(BEG END LEVEL)} for
the section around point.
@item
@code{(latex-structure-heading-title POS)} returns the title of the
heading at POS@.
@item
@code{(latex-structure-item-at &optional POS)} returns a plist with the
list around POS, all of its items, and the index of the item at
POS, or nil.
@item
@code{(latex-structure-master-file)} and
@code{(latex-structure-project-files)} return the master file and all
files of the document.
@end itemize

The generated API reference in @samp{docs/api/latex-structure-api.md}
lists every function and option with its docstring.

@node Troubleshooting
@chapter Troubleshooting

@cindex troubleshooting
@cindex FAQ

@table @asis
@item A Meta-arrow key does nothing special.
Check that the mode line
shows @samp{Struct} and that point is on a heading line or inside an
item.  Text before the first @code{\item} of a list is not inside an
item.
@item The refile list misses a chapter file.
Check that the chapter is
pulled in with one of the commands in
@code{latex-structure-include-regexp} and that @code{TeX-master} names the
master file in chapter buffers.  Paths built from macros, such as
@code{\input@{\chapdir/ch1@}}, cannot be followed.
@item A refiled section has the wrong level.
Set
@code{latex-structure-refile-adjust-levels} to nil to keep levels, or
promote and demote the section afterward with @code{M-S-<left>} and
@code{M-S-<right>}.
@item AUC@TeX{} already uses a key.
Minor mode maps take priority over
the major mode map.  Rebind the key in @code{latex-structure-mode-map}
as shown in @ref{Key bindings}.
@item Evil users.
In normal state, Evil reads the Meta-arrow keys
before this package does.  The keys work in insert and Emacs
states.
@end table

